      "id": 488558,
      "username": "Nishit33",
      "name": "Nishit",
      "created_at": "2025-12-10T12:50:33.049Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I have a <strong>Query Report</strong> in ERPNext and I want to set default values for two Date filters:</p>\n<p>From Date: Today - 3M<br>\nTo Date: Today</p>\n<p>But ERPNext is not interpreting these correctly. Instead of subtracting 3 months from today’s date, it’s giving a completely wrong date like <strong>01-01-2003</strong>.</p>\n<p>What is the correct way to set default filter values 3 months back &amp; today in a Query Report ?</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/87869e/{size}.png",
      "trust_level": 1,
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
      "Reads": 32,
      "wikis": null,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_view_edit_history": true,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "version": 1,
      "last_edited_at": null,
      "edited_at": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488564,
      "username": "Omar-Abdullah",
      "name": "Omar Shaikh Al Zoor",
      "created_at": "2025-12-10T13:19:51.770Z",
      "cooked": "<p>You can use this property for the Date filter:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>default: frappe.datetime.add_months(frappe.datetime.get_today(), -3),</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>default: frappe.datetime.get_today()</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>How it will look:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">{\n\tfieldname: \"from_date\",\n\tlabel: __(\"From Date\"),\n\tfieldtype: \"Date\",\n\tdefault: frappe.datetime.add_months(frappe.datetime.get_today(), -3),\n\t//reqd: 1, optional property\n},\n{\n\tfieldname: \"to_date\",\n\tlabel: __(\"To Date\"),\n\tfieldtype: \"Date\",\n\tdefault: frappe.datetime.get_today()\n\t//reqd: 1, optional property\n},\n</code></pre>",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/df788c/{size}.png",
